<!--
  The update feed SkyGlance checks, served straight from this branch — see
  SUFeedURL in app/build-app.sh. It lives in the repository rather than on a
  host of its own so that publishing an update is a commit next to the code it
  describes, and so there is no second place to forget.

  Adding a release means: build and notarise the disk image, attach it to the
  GitHub release, run `sign_update` on the exact file that was uploaded, and add
  an <item> here with the signature it prints. The signature is over the file's
  bytes, so re-uploading a rebuilt image without updating it will leave every
  installed copy refusing the update.

  Newest first. sparkle:version is CFBundleVersion, which is what Sparkle
  compares; sparkle:shortVersionString is only what it shows a person.
-->
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle">
  <channel>
    <title>SkyGlance</title>
    <link>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/darshjoshi/skyglance-mac/main/appcast.xml</link>
    <description>What is flying over your head right now.</description>
    <language>en</language>
    <item>
      <title>0.3.0</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:20:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>300</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <ul>
          <li><b>Setup says whether a location will show anything.</b> The flight
              feeds are volunteer receivers, and whole regions — including large
              cities — have none. SkyGlance now checks before you commit, instead
              of leaving you with an empty sky and no explanation.</li>
          <li><b>Distances can be miles.</b> Defaults to whatever your Mac's
              region uses. Altitude stays in feet, as aviation does everywhere.</li>
          <li><b>Now distributed as a disk image</b>, so the app ends up in
              Applications — where macOS will actually keep running it from the
              path you can see, which is what Launch at Login depends on.</li>
          <li><b>Updates itself from now on.</b> This is the first version that
              can.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
